Company description :
Glencore is one of the world’s largest global diversified natural resource companies. Our global network comprises more than 90 offices located in over 50 countries, with over 150 mining and metallurgical sites, offshore oil production assets, farms and agricultural facilities. We employ approximately 200,000 people and it’s these people that we value above all else. They are our greatest asset. Our strategy is to maintain and build upon our position as a leading integrated producer and marketer of commodities worldwide.
Join us and let’s grow together.
Location:
This position is based in Laval or Toronto.
The employee will be allowed to work remotely in compliance with company policies
Job type :
Permanent, Full-Time
Travel :
This position requires occasional travel between our business units in Montreal East, Rouyn-Noranda, the United States, and our Toronto or Laval offices.
About the role :
In this role, you’ll be part of the Regional BAP Finance Team for the Glencore Copper North American assets division.
More specifically, you will be expected to:
Produce financial reports for Revenues, working capital, Cash flow statement and Metal inventories for the North American Copper Assets ;
Perform budget variances and explanations for revenues, freight and metal inventories ;
Responsible for submitting financial and non-financial information to the Copper Regional and Global Finance teams for all monthly deliverables of the FP&A function ;
Perform working capital analysis and the impact on financing costs ;
Perform analysis on the impact of metal price fluctuations and hedging strategies on financial results ;
Produce financial reports in regards to feed stream profile and production for our industrial assets in collaboration with operations and commercial ;
Participate in the financial processes for budgeting and business valuation of the North American Copper Assets ;
Responsible to maintain the Financial structure for revenues in SAP and in other related systems.
Do you have what it takes?
Bachelors degree in accounting or business administration in accounting or finance combined with a minimum of 3 years experience in a similar role ;
Good change management skills and the ability to adapt to a dynamic and changing environment ;
Need to be comfortable with tight deadlines ;
Good leadership skills ;
Have a collaborative approach and value developing business relationships ;
The ability to make connections between finance and operating processes, business strategies and contractual terms ;
